WEBVTT

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.840
VANELLOPE: Whoo-hoo!

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.200
Whoo!

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:12.080
And one, two, three gumballs
right on cue.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.120
Yeah, I love it
when she glitches.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.440
(ENGINES REVVING)

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.920
(VANELLOPE SNORING)

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.080
Ooh! Huh.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.120
Excuse me.
I must have fallen asleep.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.360
Oh, fun. I'm winning.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:25.600
(CRYING)

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.160
ANNOUNCER:
Vanellope takes a huge lead.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.840
No one's gonna catch her now.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:34.360
(EXCLAIMING)

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.360
She's gonna love this.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:37.840
(ENGINE REVVING)

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.720
(CHUCKLES) Right on time.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.000
What?

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.120
"Looking for something new...

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.160
"and different?

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.400
"Then take this track."
(LAUGHS)

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.160
Oh, Ralph,
you old son-of-a-gun.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.920
I'd say I got a little time
for a detour.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.120
SWATI: Whoa!

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.920
Hey, look, I think I unlocked
a new track.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.680
-Never seen that before.
-(VANELLOPE WHOOPING)

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.080
(EXCLAIMING SHAKILY)

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.200
This is awesome!

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.600
-Hey, thanks, Ralph!
-(RALPH LAUGHS)

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.320
You're welcome!

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.040
Get back up on the track,
Swati.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:12.240
You're going to lose.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.080
(STAMMERS) I can't.
It's like it's driving itself.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:20.000
Whoo! (EXCLAIMING)

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.200
What is wrong with this thing?
(GRUNTS)

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.120
(CHUCKLES) What?

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:27.040
-(GRUNTING)
-(GASPS, GRUNTS)

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:28.400
(GRUNTING)

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:29.920
-(GRUNTING)
-(GASPS)

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.440
-(YELLS) No, no!
-(GASPS)

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:33.960
RALPH: Kid!

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.560
(VANELLOPE SCREAMING)

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.400
(VANELLOPE SHRIEKS)

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.160
Oh, no, no, no, no, no!

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:44.920
RALPH: Kid! Kid!

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.680
Oh, kid, I'm so sorry,
are you okay?

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.680
VANELLOPE: Oh, my gosh.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.080
What an amazing track!

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:53.160
Thank you, Ralph! Thank you,
thank you, thank you!

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:54.360
(LAUGHS) You're welcome!

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:57.160
You know I take my duty
as your hero very seriously.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:58.240
Wait a minute.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.200
You took a serious
doody where?

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.080
(BOTH LAUGHING)

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.440
(WHISPERING)
Vanellope, get up here.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:05.360
We have a situation.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:10.400
Mr. Litwak, the Vanellope
racer wasn't working...

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.440
and I think maybe
I turned the wheel too hard.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.200
-Whoa.
-I'm real sorry.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.640
It's okay, Swati.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.400
I think I can get it back
on there pretty easy.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.720
-What did you do, Ralph?
-Nothing.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:21.880
Leave him alone.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.760
He was just trying to
make the game more exciting.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:26.760
Yeah, why don't you relax,
Taffyta? Litwak will fix it.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.040
All right, on you...
(GRUNTING)

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.320
-(NAFISA GASPS)
-Oh!

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.680
Okay. Still not a problem.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:34.120
He'll just order a new part.

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:35.440
Well, I'd order a new part...

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.160
but the company
that made Sugar Rush

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:38.320
went out of business
years ago.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.600
-(RALPH SIGHS)
-(CANDLEHEAD EXCLAIMS)

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.000
BOYD: I can try to find one
on the Internet.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.080
NAFISA: Good idea.
GIRL: Oh, me too.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.760
Good luck, that'll be like
finding a needle in a...

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.480
I found one! On ebay!

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.240
Really? How about that?

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.240
See? Those kids
have it under control.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.280
They're just gonna get another
wheel from the eboy.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.080
MR. LITWAK: Are you
kidding me? How much?

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:55.600
That's more than this game
makes in a year.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.080
Aw, I hate to say it,

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.920
but my salvage guy
is coming on Friday...

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:02.440
and it might be time to sell
Sugar Rush for parts.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:05.440
-SWATI: Aww.
-Where's he going?

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:06.960
Litwak's gonna
unplug the game.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.320
Get out of here!
Go, scram, let's go, run!

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.680
RALPH: Go, run, run, run, run!

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:10.840
-Let's go!
-JUBILEENA: Run!

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.240
(SURGE PROTECTOR WHISTLING)

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:19.040
(RUMBLING)

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.120
WYNNCHEL: Gangway!

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.280
DUNCAN: Yeah,
you heard him, gangway!

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.400
(GROANS) Stop it! No running!

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.400
What are you people doing
out of your game,

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:26.480
for Peter's sake?

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.440
The arcade is open!

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.320
(PANTING) Sugar Rush
is getting unplugged.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.320
(WHIRRING)

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.760
(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.960
-(POWERING DOWN)
-(ALL EXCLAIMING)

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:39.760
-We're homeless! (SOBBING)
-Yeah, yeah, we're homeless!

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:42.840
-Oh, what are we going to do?
-(CRYING)

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:46.160
Y'all, calm down, calm down.
Get a hold of yourselves.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.080
SUGAR RUSH CANDY:
I don't want to be gameless.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.160
(SURGE PROTECTOR GROANS)

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.000
An unplugging.
Good Lord.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.400
I haven't seen
this many gameless characters

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.480
since Space Invaders
went down.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:56.960
Um...

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.920
Where are we gonna live?

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.520
Well, you can stay here until
the arcade closes, I guess...

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:02.960
and then we'll figure out

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.120
where the heck
we're gonna put you all.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:19.000
(LADDER CLANKING)

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:21.320
Okay.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:23.360
Here we go.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:24.640
I raided Gene's fridge.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:26.840
Good news, he's got pie.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.560
Took a bunch of his pillows
and junk, too.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:31.760
I'm thinking we make a fort
up here, or like a yurt.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.680
Or we could take
these pillows...

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:34.920
If we stack them right,

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.920
we can make an igloo
out of pillows.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:40.320
Like a pillow igloo.
Pigloo. Pigloo!

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.520
So what do you think, kid?

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:44.720
Fort, yurt, or the obvious
best choice, pigloo?

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:49.120
I can't believe I don't have
a game anymore.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:52.520
I mean, like,
what am I gonna do all day?

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:55.000
What? Come on,
are you kidding?

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.760
You sleep in, you do no work,

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:58.880
then you go to Tapper's
with me every night.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.040
I've literally
just described paradise.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.840
But I loved my game.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.000
Oh, come on.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.360
You were just bellyaching
about the tracks

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:06.480
being too easy.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:08.640
No, that doesn't mean
I didn't love it.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:12.160
Yeah, sure,
it was kind of predictable...

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:16.360
but still I never really knew
what might happen in a race.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.680
And it's that,
it's that feeling,

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:21.240
that not-knowing-what's-
coming-next feeling.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:26.000
That's the stuff.
That feels like life to me.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.160
And if I'm not a racer,
Ralph...

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.360
what am I?

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:33.760
Well, you're my best friend.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:35.160
That's not enough.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:36.320
Hey.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:37.960
No, I just...

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:41.280
I'm sorry,
I know I'm being weird.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:47.000
I think maybe I just need to
be alone right now.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.120
Oh.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:50.320
Okay.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:54.120
I'll meet you over at Tapper's
in a little while, I guess.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:56.840
If you want.

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:00.080
FELIX: All right, now...

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:01.360
we found some good homes

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.320
for so many of our chums
from Sugar Rush...

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:05.160
and we're just hoping
a few more of you

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:06.240
will open your doors...

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.440
and your hearts
to those in need.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:11.120
Well, I suppose
that large green olive

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.880
will fit in nicely
with my decor.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:15.120
I'm a sour ball.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:17.920
Well, beggars can't be
choosers, can they?

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:19.760
Come along, condiment.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:21.400
(SIGHS) Mm-kay.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:24.560
Marvelous.
That just leaves the racers.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:26.800
We're, like, adorable.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:28.560
You sure are.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:30.800
So, any takers?

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:33.400
(ALL HUMMING HESITATINGLY)

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:34.960
FELIX: Um...

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.600
Anyone?

